title: Activating a Vocabulary
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Two ways to opt a tiddler into a vocab's markers:

# ''Type field'': `type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Legacy-Glyphs`. A startup-module patch keeps the tiddler as a single `.tid` file on disk.
# ''Pragma'': `\importcustom [tag[vocab/legacy-glyphs]]` at the top of a tiddler. The filter runs over `[all[shadows+tiddlers]]` automatically, so you don't need to spell the shadow-inclusion prefix yourself, marker tiddlers are almost always shipped as plugin shadows.

vocab/default is always active. With no `;vocab=` parameter, only Default markers fire.

!! `disable-core-rules` semantics

When a vocab declaring `disable-core-rules` activates, the listed TW core rules are removed from the parser's rule set ''for that tiddler only'' (via `parser.amendRules("except", ...)`). The amendment runs before pragma parsing, so a user `\rules only ...` / `\rules except ...` pragma can still amend further.

This is how a vocab claims syntax that would otherwise collide with TW core. Fountain disables `heading list` so `! action` and `# section` belong to the vocab; Markdown disables `strikethrough codeinline list underscore table` so its own markers own those line-starts and bracket pairs.